\section*{Conformal stress improvement in the finite-scaling-support operational framework}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. The designated four-dimensional scale-invariant operational QFT class is claimed to admit a traceless stress-tensor improvement and unbroken local conformal Ward identities.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Result 1.} The framework assumes vacuum-generated four-dimensional Wightman fields and their adjoints on a common invariant polynomial domain, positive translation spectrum, Poincar\'e covariance, graded locality, and a vacuum invariant under continuous dilations. Original field labels decompose algebraically into finite scaling support,
\[
 \mathcal F=\bigoplus_{\Delta\in\Sigma}\mathcal F_\Delta,
\]
where real \(\Sigma\) is bounded below and locally finite and each Lorentz-stable grade is finite-dimensional. Adjoints preserve grades and differentiation raises dimension by one. A fixed covariant isotone local net contains closed affiliated realizations; new physical fields require arbitrarily small localization, all joint finite-length distributions, compatible domains/adjoints, and affiliation in that original net. The original stress tensor is symmetric and conserved, with translation/Lorentz Ward identities, and a virial field generates dilations through \(D_\mu=x^\nu T_{\mu\nu}-V_\mu\), \(T^\mu{}_{\mu}=\partial^\mu V_\mu\). In this specified framework the claim supplies a Hermitian physical dimension-two scalar \(L\) with
\[
 \partial^\mu V^{(3)}_\mu=\Box L,\qquad
 t_{\mu\nu}=T^{(4)}_{\mu\nu}
 +\tfrac13(\partial_\mu\partial_\nu-\eta_{\mu\nu}\Box)L,
\]
symmetric, conserved, traceless, and carrying the same affine Ward charges. Conformal-Killing currents \(X^\nu t_{\mu\nu}\) extend the unbroken local Ward action. This theorem retains finite scaling support and the operational field-membership conditions. The common invariant domain must contain
\[
 D_{\mathrm{old}}=\operatorname{span}\{\Omega,A_1\cdots A_n(h)\Omega:
 n<\infty,\ h\in\mathcal S((\mathbb R^4)^n)\},
\]
with the original fields acting by their original insertion rule. Here $h$ is an arbitrary joint test kernel, without a finite-rank restriction. Homogeneous scaling has convention
\[
 U_D(s)A_\Delta(x)U_D(-s)=e^{s\Delta}A_\Delta(e^s x).
\]

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Bounded null-cut identities and two-horizon spectral comparisons isolate a localizable scalar wave. Quadratic-charge and time-cone estimates establish compatible local products, enabling stress improvement without changing Poincare charges; the conclusion concerns local currents rather than a global action on the entire net.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The designated four-dimensional scale-invariant operational QFT class is claimed to admit a traceless stress-tensor improvement and unbroken local conformal Ward identities. The question retains these same parameters and conventions. Within these assumptions, this is a claimed affirmative answer to the stated question.

